rmat(record)\n    ...\n```\n\nWait: `record.message` is set by Formatter.format as `record.getMessage()`. After super().format, record.message is the truncated message (on the copy). The newline alignment uses record.message from original record — but super().format on copy sets copy.message, original record.message remains unset (None). Actually `logging.Formatter.format` sets `record.message = record.getMessage()` at start. If original record.message was previously set by another handler (e.g., full handler earlier), it remains full message — the alignment code uses `record.message` (original), and msg is truncated copy's formatted text. Then `msg.find(record.message)` returns -1 and prefix = msg[:-1]... bad. Use `record.message` from the copy instead. Let me use the working record variable `record` after reassignment; since super().format(record) sets record.message to truncated, use that variable. So the alignment code referencing `record.message` refers to local variable — good, since copy has message set.\n\nBut if no truncation, record is original and super sets message = full. Fine.\n\nAlso empty message case guard: `if \"\\n\" in msg and record.message`.\n\nTruncation helper:\n\n```python\n_OMISSION_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"\n\ndef _truncate_message(message, max_chars):\n    if len(message) <= max_chars:\n        return message\n    budget = max_chars - len(_OMISSION_MARKER)\n    head = (budget + 1) // 2\n    tail = budget - head\n    return message[:head] + _OMISSION_MARKER + message[len(message) - tail:]\n```\n\nNote budget could be negative if max_chars < len(marker)=15; but min 32 ensures budget>=17. Fine.\n\nValidation: max_message_chars not None → must be int (not bool) and >= 32 else ValueError.\n\nAlso need `import copy`.\n\nNow setup:\n\n```python\ndef _setup_logger() -> None:\n    ...\n    fmt = NewLineFormatter(\n        _FORMAT,\n        datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT,\n        use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(),\n        max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS,\n    )\n```\n\nNow stats logger: `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`.\n\nLet me check current environ.py to confirm the attribute exists with name DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS and that it's int_or_none_min. Read environ.py's relevant part.\n\nAlso I need the exact text for edits. Do the patches now; first read current environ.py edited region and stats_logger lines around 115-130 exact indentation (from evidence: lines with 16 spaces `logger.info(m)`).\n\nLet me do it in one action: read environ grep, then apply edits to logger and stats. But edits depend on exact text; I have enough from evidence for logger and stats.\n\nLogger edits (replace_text_batch):\n1. import copy: old \"import datetime\\nimport logging\\nmultiprocessing\" → new \"import copy\\nimport datetime\\nimport logging\". Careful: file has \"import datetime\\nimport logging\\nimport multiprocessing\\n\".\n2. Formatter __init__ signature + validation.\n3. format method.\n4. _setup_logger fmt.\n\nLet me craft.\n\nEdit 1 old:\n```\nimport datetime\nimport logging\nimport multiprocessing\n```\nnew:\n```\nimport copy\nimport datetime\nimport logging\nimport multiprocessing\n```\n\nEdit 2 old:\n```\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        fmt: str,\n        datefmt: str | None = None,\n        high_precision: bool = False,\n        use_color: bool = False,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n```\nnew adds max_message_chars keyword-only: since 4 positional params exist, add `*, max_message_chars: int | None = None`. \n\nnew:\n```\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        fmt: str,\n        datefmt: str | None = None,\n        high_precision: bool = False,\n        use_color: bool = False,\n        *,\n        max_message_chars: int | None = None,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        if max_message_chars is not None and (\n            